      "currentVersionReleaseDate": "2026-08-21T22:03:27Z",
      "releaseNotes": "Bug fixes\nImproved Presets design. You can now save your cameras and lenses. Your existing preset information remains unchanged.\nSettings display improvements",
      "version": "2.3",
      "wrapperType": "software",
      "currency": "GBP",
      "description": "Designed by a photographer, for photographers.\nBuilt with one goal: reliable and precise exposure measurement for both digital and analog workflows.\n\nWhether you shoot film or digital, this app gives you full control over exposure with a clean, professional set of tools.\n\nKey Features\n\n• Incident and reflected-light metering\n\n• Two interface styles to match your workflow\n\n• Spot metering directly from the camera view\n\n• Full manual control over aperture, shutter speed, ISO, and exposure compensation in 1/3-stop increments\n\n• Range: 4 hours to 1/8000 s, f/1.0 to f/512, and ISO 0.8 to 409,600\n\n• Aperture priority (Av) and shutter priority (Tv)\n\n• Auto ISO or ISO lock\n\n• Reciprocity correction for long film exposures\n\n• Sensitivity down to −2.5 EV, ideal for low-light scenes\n\n• Save and review exposure data\n\n• Read exposure data from photos in your library\n\n• Average multiple measurements for greater accuracy\n\nAdvanced Tools\n\n• Hyperfocal-distance calculator\n\n• Five presets for camera, lens, ISO, filter, and film\n\n• EV display with an analog scale or numerical reading\n\n• f/Tools integration\n\n• Integration with the professional mySpotmeter app\n\nImportant\n\nFor accurate incident-light metering, a diffuser must be placed over the front camera.\nWithout a diffuser, readings will behave as reflected-light measurements.\n\nAbout\n\nThis app is built and maintained by an independent photographer and developer.\nIt is the tool I personally use and continuously refine.\n\nIf you have suggestions or need help, feel free to contact me:\ndavidquiles@me.com",
